## Effect and evidence

This refines L-S05/L-S06/L-S10. People and agents must discover recorded work, inspect session and cost evidence, and distinguish a large feed representation from physical storage consumption. Preserve that useful work. Remove per-feed physical-file sums, read-triggered legacy backfill, repeated independent measurement scans, and suppression of storage failure as absent history. Shared batches make a physical file an invalid measure of any single feed. No new persistent measurement index is needed.

The observed `sourceStatus` returns `{exists,bytes}` from physical source files. `statementLogInformationPath` separately counts row identities. FeltOS divides those separately obtained values and can turn the result into a work-ledger obligation through `obsticulationObservationsOfFeedEntropy`. The existing Data function describes this ratio as a proxy statistic, not a proven conservation law. The old representation and field names are migration evidence; neither the ratio nor a file layout establishes theoretical truth.

The content-bound [consumer evidence](evidence/2026-09-27-journal-feed-measurement/consumers.json) records the inspected source and search scope. The Gemini Notebook function with the same name is unrelated and is excluded. The list is a fabrication input aid, not a permanent manually maintained registry; generation must revalidate bindings and discover changed consumers.

## Measurement contract

**L-M01 — Feed custody and availability.** Retain the public `sourceStatus(log)` operation on the owning journal and existing facade, but replace its ambiguous result with the closed immutable object `{exists,retainedEvents,admittedEvents,pendingEvents,blockedEvents,representationBytes,representationEncoding}`. Counts and bytes are nonnegative safe integers. `representationEncoding` is exactly `metroplat.journal.admitted-witness-jsonl.v1`. `exists` means at least one verified retained witness has the selected ordinary membership or selected unique virtual feed. It does not mean causal readiness, authority to act, or presence of a physical dated file. An artifact-only batch or an obstruction whose witness/membership is unknown cannot manufacture a feed.

Count distinct event IDs within that feed. Partition its retained witnesses into admitted, pending and blocked using L-S05's existing causal laws; a contradiction that prevents a lawful partition is source-corrupt, not an arbitrary priority rule. Thus retainedEvents equals the other three counts' sum. Historical blocking without a witness remains preserved at root scope under L-S01 and is not silently assigned to an invented feed. Duplicate custody entries do not increase event counts. A unique event participates through L-S02's virtual feed without requiring a dated projection.

Verified absence returns exists false and zero counts/bytes. Pending-only or blocked-only custody returns exists true and zero admitted representation bytes, with the appropriate nonzero count. Corruption, incomplete scanning, permission errors, unsupported storage and capacity overflow must raise the declared internal storage diagnostic; they must not return this successful absent object. Map diagnostics through L-J06 at remote boundaries. No status result includes physical paths, batch sizes or another feed's counts.

**L-M02 — Exact representation bytes.** Select precisely the feed's admitted witnesses from the protected view, deduplicate by event ID and order by ordinal event ID. For each, use the existing verifier's normalized witness value, serialize with the existing canonicalJson law, encode UTF-8, and append one LF. representationBytes is the exact sum of those line lengths. This is a defined logical representation even when no such projection file exists. It excludes custody wrappers, unrelated entries, standalone artifact bodies, pending/blocked witnesses and directory overhead. Witness-contained source values remain part of the witness representation. No alternate serializer or character-count shortcut is permitted. Retain original historical source values separately under L-S01; normalization here does not rewrite them.

Equivalent membership and admitted witnesses yield the same measurement despite batch grouping, duplicate physical custody, filesystem block allocation or migration. Multiple feeds can each measure the same witness; summing their representationBytes is not root disk usage. Do not reuse the removed `bytes` field as an alias with changed meaning.

**L-M03 — Physical accounting.** Physical retained-source bytes are an operator/root-custody measurement: sum exact regular-file lengths over the deduplicated recognized immutable batches and unique-slot files in one protected complete view. Count a shared file once. Exclude maintenance lock files, temporary files, derived projections and filesystem allocation overhead. Keep this measurement inside the host maintenance interface under root-level authority; do not add it to feed responses or infer authority from possession of a feed handle. The host profile and remaining storage interface order must bind its concrete entrypoint. No per-feed physical attribution is fabricated by dividing a shared batch evenly or assigning it to the first feed.

**L-M04 — One observation for information and size.** Extend `statementLogInformationPath`'s successful information value with L-M01's named fields, retaining its existing kind and row/identity fields. Compute both sets from the same protected source view and same admitted selection inside one operation. Its rows, uniqueStatements, duplicateStatements, entropyUnits and identities retain the existing statementIdentity/row-fold laws. entropyUnits remains a count of unique statement identities, explicitly a proxy unit. It is not Shannon entropy or a measurement of thermodynamic cost.

Neither a public status call followed by a second scan nor a nested public lock acquisition satisfies this requirement. The System implementation passes its protected view internally to the row fold and measurement functions. Callers needing both size and information consume this one value. Generation must show which existing row-fold path it reuses; do not implement a second EAVT or causal law.

## Consumer migration

**L-M05 — Ratio and obligations.** Feed census and agent-session token-usage readouts use the joint information observation. Replace bytesOnDisk with representationBytes and carry representationEncoding alongside it. Retain the existing pure feedEntropyReading calculation and its threshold of 4096 as an explicitly named representation-density policy; rename misleading parameter descriptions, without changing its mathematical truth-table law. The threshold is a policy inherited for this proxy, not an empirically established physical-storage limit. Old physical-byte observations remain historical and must not be compared as measurements of the new encoding.

The ratio is representationBytes / entropyUnits only when entropyUnits is positive. When it is zero, omit the ratio and do not call the ratio policy or generate an over-bound obligation; preserve any pending/blocked counts in the readout. Never report zero-information custody as proof that the policy was satisfied. A measurement failure prevents the census/obligation derivation from completing and is returned as an obstruction, not as an empty set of obligations.

Migrate `feedEntropyOverBound`, the token-usage sourceLog value/evidence, and the pure obligation text/evidence together. An over-bound proposal must identify the encoding, representation bytes, proxy units, ratio and threshold. Its text describes an oversized admitted representation; it must not claim physical disk exhaustion or authorize deletion. Preserve the existing work-ledger proposal/admission and authority boundaries. Previously recorded obligations keep their original evidence; this order does not retract or reinterpret them.

**L-M06 — Other byte readouts.** The plate-promotion readout replaces logBytes with representationBytes and representationEncoding. The recorded Claude-session fleet entry replaces bytes with those explicit fields; migrate the closed fleet session schema in the same source patchset. Preserve session identities, observation counts, goals, obligations and the existing session judgment. The generator must inspect all producers and consumers of that schema; transcript-file bytes in other capabilities remain physical transcript measurements and are not mechanically renamed.

**L-M07 — Absence and failure consumers.** Migrate all journal sourceStatus consumers identified in the bound evidence: MetroPlat resource derivation; computer-code-development monitoring and agent services; FeltOS work service, context, feed readouts, Claude fleet and token usage; and computer-inference pricing. An exists guard may still skip a genuinely absent feed. For present pending/blocked-only feeds, consumers must carry an explicit incomplete/obstructed readout through their existing result/error surface; they cannot label this as no recorded work, a complete empty context, a complete zero-cost result or permission to execute again. A read of the admitted portion may be offered only with that incompleteness explicit.

Audit the actual `try/catch` and result construction following each guard. Several currently catch every scan error and return undefined or an empty array; some context construction deliberately returns fewer inputs on unreadable history. Remove that suppression for the declared storage diagnostics and preserve the error through operation presentation. This is necessary for work selection to know when its evidence is unavailable. Retain intentional handling of unrelated optional materials; do not turn every absent supplemental note into a storage failure. L-M09/L-M10 below fix the diagnostic and result/error mapping. The integrated fabrication order must bind the exact changed call sites, including intervening folds and catches; it must not leave these mappings to the generator's invention.

**L-M08 — Removal and independent observations.** The generated integrated patchset removes sourceByteLengthInternal's physical per-feed sum and the file-path-based scanSourceFilesInternal route as required by L-S06, and removes all product consumers of sourceStatus(...).bytes. The new implementation cannot preserve legacy read-through writes as a compatibility path. Revalidate the complete affected consumers and exports under L-S10; a search result alone is not proof of architectural retirement.

Commit independent observations before generation: two unrelated feeds in one physical batch; the same witness in multiple feeds; duplicate physical witness custody; exact multibyte UTF-8 lengths; a unique-slot-only virtual feed; pending-only custody becoming admitted after its required cause arrives; historical blocking; source corruption and read denial reaching the caller; an attempted concurrent append between census components; and an over-bound obligation whose text/evidence names the new measure. Verify the fleet's closed schema and actual readout, plus the absence of physical batch paths/size from feed responses. Exercise empty and zero-information cases without fabricated affirmative policy readings. Compare root physical totals with physical files independently and demonstrate they differ from a sum over feed representations where sharing occurs.

## Closed obstruction path

**L-M09 — System storage diagnostics.** Add the System-owned module `src/journal/diagnostics.mjs` and its package export in the integrated generated patchset. It exports `journalUnavailable(reason, diagnostics)` and `isJournalUnavailable(value)`. The constructor accepts only L-J06's seven exact public reasons. Invalid reason construction throws TypeError; do not normalize unknown strings into an invented public reason. The returned Error has name `JournalUnavailable`, code `JOURNAL_UNAVAILABLE`, reason equal to the admitted string, and message exactly `journal unavailable: <reason>`. Freeze those public fields. The predicate recognizes only locally constructed instances using private instance membership, not caller-supplied code, reason or message properties. A JSON object with these fields cannot create a trusted host diagnostic or any authority.

Retain detailed host diagnostics in module-private weak storage for the lifetime of the error; they are not enumerable fields, Error.cause, public JSON or message suffixes. The constructor's private diagnostic input may identify the internal operation/failure and original exception. No public serializer receives that private value. This is immediate in-process diagnostic custody, not a claim that a failed journal durably recorded its own failure. A later host diagnostic sink needs its own admitted destination and must not turn failure to log into successful execution. Callers that have a nonstorage failure retain their existing error handling; do not classify all thrown exceptions as journal failures.

The storage boundary translates actual host events before they escape it:

| Observed failure | Public reason | Private distinction retained |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Verified malformed or wrong-address recognized source, conflicting source representation | source-corrupt | Source family and verifier diagnostic |
| Required causal/artifact evidence absent or blocked; required complete feed has pending/blocked witnesses | evidence-unavailable | Missing/blocked references or incomplete selection |
| Bounded scan, traversal, count or byte capacity exceeded | resource-limit | Capacity name and observed limit |
| Lock contention or rejected reentrant public operation | maintenance-busy | Contention versus reentrancy |
| Host cannot provide the selected exclusion/durability semantics | storage-unsupported | Unsupported mechanism/profile |
| Root binding changed, unreadable source, other host I/O error, or unmigrated legacy root | storage-unavailable | In particular migration-required remains private |
| Publication may already have become visible before a failed acknowledgment | publication-uncertain | Publication stage and original failure |

Publication uncertainty takes precedence over the lower-level failure reason once visibility is possible. A generic EIO does not establish either absence or completed publication. Pure command/identity refusal and authorization denial remain their own earlier outcomes under L-J06; they do not call this constructor. Unique admission translates a recognized diagnostic to the exact `{disposition:"unavailable",reason}` result only at its declared boundary. A raw error not yet classified by its owning layer cannot be mistaken for an unavailable record, an absent slot, or a grant.

**L-M10 — Complete reads and concrete consumer outcomes.** A bare array, count, projection or context implies a complete answer unless its existing type explicitly says otherwise. Therefore the ordinary public `read`, `scan`, `scanCausal`, whole-feed projections and complete date/territory folds must verify the selected source set is complete before invoking the first caller fold or producing a successful value. Use the same L-S04 gate/view for that check and fold. Pending or blocked witnesses in that selection raise the L-M09 evidence-unavailable diagnostic. Do not require unrelated feeds to be complete for a per-feed read; verified corruption preventing a complete root scan still refuses under L-S03. Exact-reference/as-of operations require their specified closure, not every unrelated pending witness. This is a selection rule, not a replacement causal law.

L-M01 status and L-M04 information are explicitly custody/availability observations and remain able to report partial admitted information with their pending/blocked counts. They use internal protected-view folds and never call a public complete-read method recursively. Preserve that usable inspection capability during outages. Adding a general partial-work execution mode is outside this order. A status guard followed by a scan does not confer a durable absence fact; each scan checks its own protected selection. No caller may cache an earlier exists=false as permission for an external effect.

The following mappings are mandatory across both direct function use and registered operation use. For all rows, `isJournalUnavailable(error)` must be rethrown before a broad catch can substitute a success value. Existing successful codomains remain unchanged except the explicit measurement field changes in L-M05/L-M06.

| Consumer | Complete evidence required for | Result when required evidence is unavailable |
| --- | --- | --- |
| computer-code-development `monitoring/operations.mjs` | RPC stage collection | Throw the recognized diagnostic; do not skip the affected stage/date as empty |
| computer-code-development `agent/service.mjs` | Skill candidates, skill proposals, executed actuation requests | Throw; no undefined readout or empty executed-request set |
| computer-inference `openai/pricing/operations.mjs` | Complete cost readout | Throw; no undefined/zero-cost substitute |
| MetroPlat `resources/read-write-verbs.mjs` | Derive state, record or content from a feed | Throw before publishing a replacement projection; do not fall back to stale content or return absent |
| FeltOS `work/service.mjs` | Subject work, governance, milestones, work-item views, duties and agent-work dispatch folds | Throw; no skipped feed, empty standing, undefined governance, or partially collected executable work disguised as a successful readout with malformed=1 |
| FeltOS `agents/context.mjs` | Work-ledger inputs, distinct cells, derived session/work context | Propagate through helper folds and resource.read; do not return fewer journal-derived inputs as a complete context |
| FeltOS Claude fleet service | Hook state, claim deltas, bundles and recorded fleet readout | Throw; no empty sessions/deltas/bundles substitute |
| FeltOS token-usage service | Complete token/cost collector and joint measurement | Throw; no complete zero-usage substitute |
| FeltOS feed readout | Feed/plate projection and census used to derive work obligations | Throw for required-source failure; do not count an obstructed feed as absent or produce a partial successful obligation list |

`sourceStatus` can still distinguish genuinely absent custody. If a later complete read finds no admitted rows because custody is pending/blocked, the protected check throws rather than relying on that guard. For helper calls not named above, follow the actual call path to the row fold and outer result construction; moving a catch to a wrapper does not satisfy the mapping. Source I/O classification belongs to Systems; lower-layer Code/Networking transformations must not import this module upward.

For governed RPC, the existing `dispatch` obstruction path is the result carrier: ok=false, existing phase preserved, no successful value. Its reason contains the sanitized journal message (existing explanatory prefixes for authorization/coordination witnessing and post-execution witnessing remain permissible). Do not retry the handler or run dependent work because an obstruction was returned. If outcome witnessing fails after the handler ran, preserve the witnessing phase and the existing statement that execution completed but witnessing failed; never rewrite that as 'not executed'. These receipts describe RPC execution only, not independent acceptance of an external effect.

The existing CLI mapping returns code 1, empty stdout and sanitized stderr for that obstruction. The existing ordinary operation HTTP mapping returns an action error with HTTP 422 and that sanitized diagnostic, never HTTP 200 with empty successful data. Preserve this existing transport mapping for this work family; do not infer a new retry policy from the HTTP code. The MCP tools/call mapping uses the existing mcpToolErrorResult/mcpToolRefusalResult, retaining error status, phase and sanitized reasons. A storage exception escaping direct MCP resource/prompt resolution uses the existing -32603 failure response with the sanitized message, never a success with omitted content. Raw filesystem messages and stack traces cannot be put into public reasons by any of these routes. Test actual wrappers; an Error class alone does not prove the receiving response.

Authentication remains upstream and unresolved as already stated in L-S08. This error mapping neither enables remote personal-work routes nor closes the existing process-subject fallback. Likewise, generic errors outside the storage family are not claimed to be sanitized by this change.

Private acceptance additionally commits failures at the actual consumer fold and route: direct function throws, RPC ok=false with no value, CLI nonzero/empty stdout, ordinary HTTP action error, MCP tool error and MCP resource failure. Place a distinctive private filesystem string in the host failure and verify it appears in none of those public outputs. Present a spoofed plain object diagnostic and confirm it is not recognized as a host instance. Verify zero handler calls when evidence fails before execution, one handler call with witnessing obstruction when the final record fails, and no automatic second execution. Introduce pending custody after an initial status read and demonstrate the complete scan refuses before invoking its callback. Demonstrate partial information remains inspectable through L-M04 with explicit counts.

This refinement closes feed measurement meaning, consumer failure outcomes and transport mappings. It does not close the host capacity profile, trusted journal identity, domain registration, or the integrated source-view interface and source inventory. No product generation, migration, deployment, or operating assistant acceptance is claimed here.
